  "description": "Shenora's Chromium engine, through CEF, for an app that ships its own browser engine instead of WebView2. UseChromium is a shell of the kit's own: CEF's windows with frameless chrome, real caption buttons and Snap Layouts, file drops with real paths, native file dialogs, the clipboard, secondary windows, crash reload and dev-server hot reload, with IPC over a transport that needs no code in the renderer. ChromiumEngine and ChromiumChildBrowser embed a page in a window the host owns, which is how Shenora.Windows hosts one beside its WebView2 control. CEF itself is not in the package: the app's build fetches the pinned CEF build, checks its SHA-1, and lays the app out, on Windows beside CEF's launcher with the kit's shim, which is what gives Chromium its sandbox, and on macOS as an app bundle whose helpers sandbox each subprocess. Reference it from the app's own project, with a RuntimeIdentifier and an assembly named <App>.App. Windows (x64, arm64) and macOS (x64, arm64), where the build makes an app bundle.",
